	doi = {10.1109/SPEC.2016.7846140},
	abstract = {Performance of inductively coupled electric vehicle (EV) charging systems is significantly affected by the misalignments between charging pads (coils). This paper investigates the use of inductor-capacitor-inductor (LCL) and capacitor-inductor (CL) compensations in wireless charging systems, based on inductive power transfer (IPT), to achieve high tolerance towards pad-misalignments. A three phase bi-directional inductive power transfer (BD-IPT) system is studied with both LCL and CL compensations, and a mathematical model is developed to investigate its performance under pad-misalignments. Theoretical results are presented in comparison with simulations, verifying the proposed concept and the accuracy of the developed model. Both theoretical and simulation results indicate that the adoption of combined compensations is a promising approach to achieve high tolerance for pad-misalignments during wireless charging.},
